cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mdcx: verified conversion of document collections to queryable Markdown"
message: "If you use this software in published work, please cite the entry below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ellena
    given-names: Jorge
repository-code: "https://github.com/jorgell23-sys/mdcx"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22015991
abstract: >-
  Converts complete document collections to Markdown and measures each conversion
  against the text the original exposes, read with a library independent from the
  engine that produced it, so that fidelity is reported rather than assumed; over
  the collection used during development, 99 documents and 1,144,553 reference
  tokens, coverage reached 99.948%. The corpus is packaged with its index and the
  provenance of every passage into a single file encrypted with AES-256-GCM, and
  served to agents through the Model Context Protocol. Retrieval merges word
  matching with a multilingual embedding model by reciprocal rank, which reaches
  documents that share the subject of a query without sharing its vocabulary or
  its language. Answering one query through the package cost 435 model tokens
  against the 2,265,488 required to read the same collection in full.
keywords:
  - document conversion
  - markdown
  - retrieval
  - model context protocol
  - provenance
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.10.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
